{"latest_judgment":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_33_277727373#13_627992154","relevance":2,"reason":"This student/children-oriented animal-testing essay lists concrete actions such as buying cruelty-free products, stopping use of animal-tested products, supporting groups like PETA, and using alternatives, but it is generic advice rather than a teen-led action document.","learned":"Student-facing essays can support actions teens can take: buy cruelty-free, stop using animal-tested products, and support alternatives or organizations."},"action":{"op":"next","qid":"q1005","reason":"The cruelty-free/student query has already produced one grade-3 result and another partially useful result, so continuing may find more student or teen action evidence."}}
{"request":{"op":"next","qid":"q1005"},"response":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_15_1712296447#7_3409221057","ok":true,"op":"next","qid":"q1005","rank":3,"snippet":"body to science after you die 5. Launch a campaign Conclusion \" , \"segment\": \"4. Donate your body to science after you die The main reason why scientists end up testing on animals is that it is the only way they can go about certain distinct experiments. Therefore, you can always consider leaving your body for doctors, scientists and medical <cover>students to carry out their tests using it instead of resorting to animal brutality. This will also enable you to reduce and fight against animal testing even after your death. If a good number of people leave their bodies for science, this will significantly reduce the need to hurt animals in various experiments. 5. Launch a campaign If you have the resources and the capability, you can always launch cruelty-free </cover>campaigns. Launching a campaign does not mean you have to be violent in any way. There are many ways you can achieve your goal. For instance, you can incorporate a day of the month which you used to hand out brochures and education materials that advocate against animal testing and brutality.\" , \"start_char\": 3768.000000 , \"title"}}
