{"latest_judgment":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_11_1154651207#5_2317126182","relevance":1,"reason":"The document is an anti-vivisection campaign page that mentions research students and asks readers to support a campaign, educate others, and spread posters, but it is not about teens and does not provide evidence of teen-led action to stop animal testing.","learned":"Animal experimentation/vivisection wording still retrieves general campaign material rather than teen-specific actions."},"action":{"op":"query","query":"(^ (+ \"boycott animal-tested products\" \"boycott products tested on animals\" \"purchase cruelty free products\") (+ students teens teenagers))","reason":"Search for distinctive action phrasing from the strongest student-authored result to find more dedicated teen/student evidence advocating boycotts and cruelty-free purchasing."}}
{"request":{"op":"query","query":"(^ (+ \"boycott animal-tested products\" \"boycott products tested on animals\" \"purchase cruelty free products\") (+ students teens teenagers))"},"response":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_48_784096458#5_1416309427","ok":true,"op":"next","qid":"q1015","rank":2,"snippet":"{ \"docid\": \"msmarco_v2.1_doc_48_784096458#5_1416309427\" , \"end_char\": 3659.000000 , \"headings\": \"The darker side of cosmetic testing The darker side of cosmetic testing<cover>Students grapple with key issues Around the web \" , \"segment\": \"Plenty of organizations, such as PETA, have lists of companies that do and don’t test on animals. If you boycott animal tested products, </cover>these companies will be forced to change the way they test. Finally, there is an enormous cost to testing on animals. Do you really want your tax dollars going to labs to perform tests that sometimes don’t even work? Labs need money to do research on the testing and keep the animals (food and shelter). It is practically like paying for animals to be killed. Seems pretty pointless, right? Every day, many animals are harmed or killed in labs all across the country, just so we can have what we want. I’m not saying that products shouldn’t be tested; they should just be tested in a way that is less harmful to animals.\" ,","skipped":[{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_48_784096458#0_1416301827","rank":1,"relevance":3}]}}
