{"latest_judgment":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_48_784096458#5_1416309427","relevance":3,"reason":"This is another segment of the student-authored 'The darker side of cosmetic testing' article. It directly supports student action against animal testing by saying students addressed the issue and urging boycotts of animal-tested products to force companies to change testing practices. It is repeated evidence from the same article already found, but still directly relevant.","learned":"The eighth-grade student article also argues that boycotting animal-tested products can pressure companies to change how they test."},"action":{"op":"query","query":"(^ (+ kids children teens teenagers students) \"animal testing\" (+ petition petitions signatures campaigned))","reason":"Move away from duplicate segments and search for youth or student petition/campaign evidence against animal testing."}}
{"request":{"op":"query","query":"(^ (+ kids children teens teenagers students) \"animal testing\" (+ petition petitions signatures campaigned))"},"response":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_17_2790273811#8_3021549045","ok":true,"op":"query","qid":"q1016","rank":1,"snippet":"Boris Kiriyenko John Prescott References \" , \"segment\": \"He changed his name and became Buddhist and vegetarian. He returned to England in the 1970s and enjoyed a hugely successful music career, starting a band called “Slam!” ( a parody of Wham! ). This shot him to fame at once. At the end of the 1970s, the band split up and he started a solo career. His first solo album, \\\"Firelight\\\", went platinum and he won several awards and released the single \\\"Something for the <cover>Children\" at Christmas time in 1986, with all funds given to charity. Cray campaigned for several issues, including saving the rainforests, ending world debt and banning animal testing. </cover>His tireless work for charity earned him a knighthood in 1990. The rich superstar then branched into hotels, television, and even started developing \"Gameslayer\", the most advanced and realistic game console of its time. However, despite his charitable work and beliefs, Cray had a darker and more sinister side to him;\" , \"start_char\": 4915.000000 , \"title\": \"List of Alex Rider characters - Wikipedia\" , \"url\": \"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/"}}
