{"latest_judgment":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_06_1795391569#0_2728547097","relevance":1,"reason":"The passage is mainly a navigation/menu page listing animal-advocacy topics, including Help End Animal Testing, 50 Ways Kids Can Help Animals, and cruelty-free living. It suggests related resources but does not itself describe teen actions to stop animal testing.","learned":"Humane Decisions has related pages on ending animal testing, kids helping animals, and cruelty-free living, but navigation snippets are not direct evidence."},"action":{"op":"next","qid":"q1026","reason":"The query is centered on youth/student actions to stop or end animal testing and may retrieve more direct action pages after the navigational result."}}
{"request":{"op":"next","qid":"q1026"},"response":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_49_884204827#0_1799499220","ok":true,"op":"next","qid":"q1026","rank":3,"snippet":"donation. 5. Leave your body to science. 6. Share this page! Follow Us \" , \"segment\": \"6 Ways to Help Animals in Experiments | Action | PETA.org 6 Ways to Help Animals Suffering in Experiments Why are millions of animals STILL suffering in laboratories? There’s no justifiable reason. Companies do not need to torture animals in order to test mascara, shampoo, detergent, or other household products. Scientists do not have to torment monkeys in order to cure a disease. Educators do not need to buy fetal pigs to teach <cover>students physiology. There are easy ways to lend your voice to animals suffering in experiments, and together we can stop animal testing. Here are six ways you can help them (and if you haven’t already, join PETA’s Action Team to help even more animals!). 1. Always buy cruelty-free </cover>products. Cruelty-free cosmetics and household products abound.\" , \"start_char\": 0.000000 , \"title\": \"6 Ways to Help Animals in Experiments | Action | PETA.org\" , \"url\": \"https://www.peta.org/action/easy-ways-help-animals-used-killed-experiments/\" }","skipped":[{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_43_348846183#6_766498618","rank":2,"relevance":2}]}}
{"request":{"judgments":"29/50"}}
{"latest_judgment":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_49_884204827#0_1799499220","relevance":2,"reason":"This PETA action page is dedicated to ways to help animals in experiments and stop animal testing, listing actions such as buying cruelty-free products and joining PETA's Action Team. It mentions students in the context of dissection/physiology education, but it is general advice rather than evidence of teen-specific actions.","learned":"PETA lists concrete ways to help stop animal testing, including buying cruelty-free products, lending one's voice, joining an action team, and addressing animal use in education."},"action":{"op":"next","qid":"q1026","reason":"This query is retrieving dedicated anti-animal-testing action pages with some student/youth overlap; continuing may find a more teen- or student-specific result."}}
{"request":{"op":"next","qid":"q1026"},"response":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_15_1712296447#6_3409219485","ok":true,"op":"next","qid":"q1026","rank":6,"snippet":"to know about the operations that are going to be involved in carrying out the process. The fact is that you could be paying money to encourage the brutal torture of animals. Therefore, it is highly recommended to always donate to those charities that have <cover>cruelty free policies in place. This way, the fight against animal testing can be successful. 4. Donate your body to science after you die The main reason why scientists end up testing on animals is that it is the only way they can go about certain distinct experiments. Therefore, you can always consider leaving your body for doctors, scientists and medical students to carry out their tests using it instead of resorting to animal brutality. This will also enable you to reduce and fight against animal testing even after your death. If a good number of people leave their bodies for science, this will significantly reduce the need to hurt animals in various experiments.\" , \"start_char\": 3281.000000 , \"title\": \"How can we stop animal testing? |</cover>\" , \"url\": \"https://easyveganskincare.com/how-can-we-stop-animal-testing/\" }","skipped":[{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_43_348846183#7_766499917","rank":4,"relevance":2},{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_15_1712296447#7_3409221057","rank":5,"relevance":2}]}}
