{"latest_judgment":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_15_1712296447#6_3409219485","relevance":2,"reason":"This is a dedicated page on how to stop animal testing and lists concrete actions such as donating only to cruelty-free charities and leaving one's body to science to reduce use of animals. However, it is general advice and only mentions medical students incidentally, not teen-led action.","learned":"General anti-animal-testing guidance includes supporting cruelty-free charities and donating one's body to science as ways to reduce animal experiments."},"action":{"op":"query","query":"(^ (+ teens teenagers students \"high school\") (+ dissection vivisection \"animal testing\" experiments) (+ refuse campaign petition alternatives))","reason":"Search for student or teen actions in schools—such as refusing dissection, campaigning, petitioning, or using alternatives—which may be direct evidence of teens working to stop animal testing or animal experiments."}}
{"request":{"op":"query","query":"(^ (+ teens teenagers students \"high school\") (+ dissection vivisection \"animal testing\" experiments) (+ refuse campaign petition alternatives))"},"response":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_45_555980527#10_982777753","ok":true,"op":"query","qid":"q1027","rank":1,"snippet":"{ \"docid\": \"msmarco_v2.1_doc_45_555980527#10_982777753\" , \"end_char\": 5925.000000 , \"headings\": \"Victory: California Bans Cosmetics Tested on Animals Victory: California Bans Cosmetics Tested on Animals Dissection Animals used for dissection: Sources of dissected animals: What happens to the animals used for dissection? The effect on the environment: Types of classes in which dissection is taught: The danger to <cover>students Objecting to dissection Alternatives </cover>to dissection: The expense States that have informed student consent laws (K-12): States with Student Choice Policies: States with legislation proposing Student Choice: Passing a Student Choice Policy: \" , \"segment\": \"Talk to other students and go to the professor or department head as a group to explain your objection to dissection. Create a petition against dissection in your school and ask other students to sign it. Give copies to the department head, principal, and anyone else you think could help. Ask your parent (s) or guardian (s) to write a letter in support of your decision. If the department head or dean is similarly unresponsive, contact the national Dissection Hotline at ("}}
