{"latest_judgment":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_23_312882363#0_716443810","relevance":1,"reason":"This page is about dissection alternatives for high-school biology and mentions parents, teachers, and students being divided, but it does not describe teens taking action to stop animal testing or animal experiments.","learned":"High-school dissection-alternative pages may be adjacent but often focus on teaching resources rather than teen activism."},"action":{"op":"query","query":"(^ (+ students teens \"high school\") (+ \"refuse to dissect\" \"refusing dissection\" \"objecting to dissection\") (+ petition campaign alternatives))","reason":"Search for direct evidence of students or teens refusing dissection, petitioning, or campaigning for alternatives, which is a concrete youth action against animal use in experiments/classes."}}
{"request":{"op":"query","query":"(^ (+ students teens \"high school\") (+ \"refuse to dissect\" \"refusing dissection\" \"objecting to dissection\") (+ petition campaign alternatives))"},"response":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_45_555980527#6_982770782","ok":true,"op":"query","qid":"q1028","rank":1,"snippet":"{ \"docid\": \"msmarco_v2.1_doc_45_555980527#6_982770782\" , \"end_char\": 4310.000000 , \"headings\": \"Victory: California Bans Cosmetics Tested on Animals Victory: California Bans Cosmetics Tested on Animals Dissection Animals used for dissection: Sources of dissected animals: What happens to the animals used for dissection? The effect on the environment: Types of classes in which dissection is taught: The danger to <cover>students Objecting to dissection Alternatives </cover>to dissection: The expense States that have informed student consent laws (K-12): States with Student Choice Policies: States with legislation proposing Student Choice: Passing a Student Choice Policy: \" , \"segment\": \"Because there are more insects, there is greater use of pesticides, which can damage the water supply and food chain. Types of classes in which dissection is taught: Biology Anatomy Physiology Zoology Miscellaneous science courses The danger to students Animals used in dissection are often embalmed with formaldehyde, a chemical preservative which can damage the eyes and cause asthma attacks and bronchitis. Moreover, the chemical has been linked to cancer of the throat, lungs, and nasal passages. Symptoms of formaldehyde exposure "}}
