{"request":{"op":"query","query":"(^ \"students grapple with key issues\" (+ \"animal testing\" \"cosmetic testing\" \"tested on animals\"))"},"response":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_48_784096458#2_1416304981","ok":true,"op":"next","qid":"q1030","rank":2,"snippet":"{ \"docid\": \"msmarco_v2.1_doc_48_784096458#2_1416304981\" , \"end_char\": 2438.000000 , \"headings\": \"The darker side of cosmetic testing The darker side of <cover>cosmetic testing Students grapple with key issues</cover>Around the web \" , \"segment\": \"Even if the animals are not killed under the horrible testing conditions, most of them are killed afterwards in order to make room for the next batch of helpless animals. Over 25 million animals are ultimately killed per year from animal testing in the United States alone. ( animals.change.org) All different kinds of animals, ranging from monkeys to lab mice, are used for various types of testing. For example, eye shadow and other types of eye makeup are tested by applying them to rabbits to see if they cause irritation to a delicate eyelid. Unfortunately, if the product is harmful, the rabbits are harmed. Some form of product testing has been required ever since 1920, when a lash darkening product caused problems from eye irritation, to blindness, and even death. I understand that the technology back then wasn’t nearly as ","skipped":[{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_48_784096458#0_1416301827","rank":1,"relevance":3}]}}
