{"request":{"op":"query","query":"(^ (+ teen teens teenager \"young people\") (+ \"animal testing\" \"cosmetic testing\" \"tested on animals\") (+ \"cruelty-free\" boycott awareness campaign))"},"response":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_26_823590539#2_1608173124","ok":true,"op":"query","qid":"q1038","rank":1,"snippet":"\"The brand has a huge range of fairly priced products that are loved by many people with different skin types. It’s is a popular brand that is unfortunately not cruelty-free. FACTORS CLEAN AND CLEAR CRUELTY-FREE NO VEGAN SOME PRODUCTS GLUTEN-FREE NO ORGANIC NO Clean and Clear is one of the brands that is owned by Johnson and Johnson an American cosmetics giant. The cosmetic brand has chosen to adhere to policies that are similar to those of its parent company. Johnson and Johnson are not <cover>cruelty-free and include some form of animal testing. The brand has been focused on developing products targeting teens. </cover>Johnson and Johnson allow different brands within their portfolio to operate under different animal testing policies. Even after being acquired by Johnson and Johnson, Clean and Clear maintained its policies and does agree to test on animals’ post-production. Many of the brands owned by Johnson and Johnson are not cruelty-free including Aveeno, Neutrogena, and OGX. The market giant Johnson and Johnson state that as an international company that sells worldwide it aims to supply its products to its customers wherever they are located.\" , \"start_char\""}}
