{"latest_judgment":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_11_1154651207#4_2317124229","relevance":1,"reason":"This anti-vivisection page asks readers to support a campaign to stop animal testing and mentions research students, but it is not focused on teens or student actions and does not provide evidence of what teens have done.","learned":"Direct stop/end animal-testing queries continue to retrieve general anti-vivisection campaign pages, not teen-specific action evidence."},"action":{"op":"query","query":"(^ (+ \"students refused\" \"student refused\" \"refused to dissect\" \"refuse to dissect\") (+ frog frogs animals dissection) (+ school \"high school\"))","reason":"Look for concrete reports of students or high-school teens refusing animal dissection, a direct youth action against animal use in school experiments."}}
{"request":{"op":"query","query":"(^ (+ \"students refused\" \"student refused\" \"refused to dissect\" \"refuse to dissect\") (+ frog frogs animals dissection) (+ school \"high school\"))"},"response":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_33_119016816#13_272220044","ok":true,"op":"query","qid":"q1044","rank":1,"snippet":"\" , \"segment\": \"A person is guilty of ecoterrorism if the person commits a specified offense against property by: intimidating or coercing a person participating in an activity involving animals, plants, or natural resources; or preventing or obstructing a person involved in such an activity. The law has a provision that states a person who is on public property, or on private property with permission, and is peaceable exercising his or her constitutional rights is immune from prosecution and from civil liability under Pa. C.S. Sec. 8319. PA - Education - § 15-1523. Pupil's right of refusal; animal dissection 24 P.S. § 15-1523 This Pennsylvania law states that public or nonpublic <cover>school pupils from kindergarten through grade twelve may refuse to dissect, vivisect, incubate, capture or otherwise harm or destroy animals </cover>or any parts thereof as part of their course of instruction. Schools must notify pupils and their parents/guardians of the right to decline participation.\" , \"start_char\": 5838.000000 , \"title\": \"Pennsylvania Statutes | Animal Legal & Historical Center\" , \"url\": \"https://www.animallaw.info/statutes/us/pennsylvania\" }"}}
